      "metadata": {
        "title": "If the slit separation d increases while the wavelength and screen distance stay fixed, what happens to the double-slit fringe spacing?",
        "license": "CC BY-NC-SA",
        "licenseVersion": "4.0",
        "contentType": "Multiple Choice"
      },
      "params": {
        "question": "<p>If the slit separation d increases while the wavelength and screen distance stay fixed, what happens to the double-slit fringe spacing?</p>",
        "media": {
          "type": {
            "library": "H5P.Image 1.1",
            "subContentId": "c2f74565-6780-47c1-9853-8f53784e85a3",
            "metadata": {
              "title": "Double-slit intensity pattern with regularly spaced bright fringes.",
              "license": "CC BY-NC-SA",
              "licenseVersion": "4.0",
              "contentType": "Image"
            },
            "params": {
              "contentName": "Image",
              "alt": "Double-slit intensity pattern with regularly spaced bright fringes.",
              "decorative": false,
              "file": {
                "path": "images/ch04-two-slit-intensity.svg",
                "mime": "image/svg+xml",
                "width": 486,
                "height": 282
              }
            }
          },
          "disableImageZooming": false
        },
        "answers": [
          {
            "text": "<div>It decreases because the spacing is proportional to 1/d.</div>",
            "correct": true,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Yes—this is one of the correct choices.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "<div>It increases because the spacing is proportional to d.</div>",
            "correct": false,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Not this one. Revisit the chapter summary and try again.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "<div>It stays unchanged because only wavelength controls the pattern.</div>",
            "correct": false,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Not this one. Revisit the chapter summary and try again.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "<div>The bright and dark fringes exchange positions without changing spacing.</div>",
            "correct": false,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Not this one. Revisit the chapter summary and try again.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          }
        ],
